+- **blocker** `viz/src/statspanel.ts:659` never consumes `report.coverage`; `viz/src/statspanel.ts:309` and `viz/src/statspanel.ts:664` consequently label subset totals and distributions as “network.” This recreates the exact ADR-0030 defect: travel covers only measured lanes while the panel presents full-network scope and lane-km.
+- **blocker** `scripts/show/mkflowcurve.py:64` infers strandings from `exit_tick < horizon` instead of the contract’s explicit `stranded` field. A vehicle stranded on the final tick has `exit_tick == horizon`, is misclassified active, and causes the valid metrics document to fail the totals cross-check.
+- **should-fix** `viz/src/flowpanel.ts:256` excludes `strand` from the rate chart’s y-axis maximum, while `viz/src/flowpanel.ts:265` clamps every series. A mass-stranding burst—the primary gridlock failure signal—can therefore be silently clipped with no warning.
+- **should-fix** `scripts/whatif.py:251` treats every non-completed trip as horizon-censored. Stranded trips are also `completed: false`, so `censored_frac` at `scripts/whatif.py:271` is not the documented “still in-network at the horizon” share and overstates censoring in gridlocked runs.
+- **should-fix** `scripts/chicago/mkod.py:971` records realized freeway/through totals before profile resolution and scaling at `scripts/chicago/mkod.py:989`; unmatched flows are counted despite not being emitted, and `scale != 1` diagnostics disagree with the generated demand. ADR-0028 explicitly promises printed realized totals.
+- **should-fix** `scripts/show/mkflowcurve.py:114` establishes a new versioned JSON data model consumed at `viz/src/flowpanel.ts:36`, but no ADR records its fields or semantics. Repo rules require a consequential data-model decision to be captured; ADR-0030 currently covers only the run-report document.
+
+REVIEW-COMPLETE
